{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2138-01-05 21:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. You're here after your bronchoscopy with balloon dilation. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2138-01-05 21:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hey, doc. I’m okay, just some soreness in my throat and around the trach site. Expected that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2138-01-05 21:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. The team said you tolerated the procedure well. No breathing issues. You got Decadron during the procedure to reduce swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2138-01-05 21:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to hear. Was the biopsy part okay? Any immediate findings?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2138-01-05 21:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The biopsy was successful. No results yet — that takes a few days. Main goal was to open up the narrowed area and get tissue to check for inflammation or infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2138-01-05 21:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. I’ve had Klebsiella and Pseudomonas before — hope it’s not back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2138-01-05 21:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching for that. Your sputum cultures from past episodes showed those, but no signs of infection now — no fever or increased secretions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2138-01-05 21:57:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. What about the chest X-ray they did earlier?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2138-01-05 21:59:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No pneumothorax, which is great. Heart size a bit enlarged, but stable. Lungs clear. So, no complications from the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2138-01-05 22:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. How long will I be here?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2138-01-05 22:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely just a couple of days. We’re keeping you for pain control and monitoring. You’re on 6L oxygen via trach mask, and your saturation is 99% — excellent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2138-01-05 22:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. The oxycodone helped last time. Can I take it again if the pain flares?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2138-01-05 22:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve ordered oxycodone 5mg every 6 hours as needed. We’ll also give acetaminophen regularly to help reduce the opioid dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2138-01-05 22:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate that. Any changes to my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2138-01-05 22:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No — you’re continuing your usual meds: methotrexate, prednisone, famotidine, and inhaled tobramycin. We’re keeping everything consistent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2138-01-06 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning, Mr. ___. How’d you sleep? Pain under control?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2138-01-06 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Slept okay. Took oxycodone once last night. Still some soreness, but manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2138-01-06 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Your labs this morning show a high white count — 20.3 — but that’s likely from inflammation, not infection. Neutrophils are up, which fits with recent procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2138-01-06 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? Should we be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2138-01-06 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this point. No fever, lungs are clear, and you’re feeling stable. We’ll keep an eye on it, but it’s common after interventions like this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2138-01-06 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Any update on the second chest X-ray?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2138-01-06 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Done this morning — shows stable heart and lungs. No new fluid or collapse. Everything looks unchanged, which is what we want post-procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2138-01-06 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Glad to hear it. I’ve had so many dilations — six just last year — but this one feels smoother."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2138-01-06 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the team noted good airway patency after dilation. We’ll keep following with interventional pulmonology. They’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2138-01-06 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. Nurse said you had a little more bloody discharge from the trach — is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2138-01-06 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, usually happens for a day or two after dilation. It’s not heavy, just a bit more mucoid and tinged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2138-01-06 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. As long as it’s not increasing or bright red, we’re not concerned. Keep the site clean and monitor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2138-01-06 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Any word from rheumatology or infectious disease?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2138-01-06 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ve been consulted. Rheumatology will follow up to manage your polychondritis. ID wants to review the biopsy and prior cultures, especially with your history of resistant organisms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2138-01-06 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I know my case is complex with the SMAD4 mutation and all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2138-01-06 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It is, but we’re coordinating care. You’re doing well — no respiratory distress, walking independently, eating normally."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2138-01-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re planning for discharge tomorrow if all goes well. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2138-01-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Only took Tylenol this morning. Oxycodone not needed yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2138-01-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. We’ll send you home with a small supply of oxycodone — 10 tablets — just in case. But try to stick with Tylenol if you can."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2138-01-07 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What’s the max for Tylenol again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2138-01-07 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No more than 3 grams a day — that’s six 500mg tablets. You’re on 650mg twice daily now, so stay on that schedule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2138-01-07 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Any restrictions on activity?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2138-01-07 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No heavy lifting for a week. Otherwise, resume normal activities as tolerated. Watch for increased pain, fever, or breathing trouble — call us if those happen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2138-01-07 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-ups?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2138-01-07 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes — interventional pulmonology, rheumatology, and infectious disease all have appointments scheduled. We’ll send you the details."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2138-01-08 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning! You’re cleared for discharge. We’re just waiting on your transport."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2138-01-08 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Everything set with meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2138-01-08 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes — same as before, but oxycodone is now 7.5mg every 4 hours as needed. Only take it if Tylenol isn’t enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2138-01-08 07:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And prednisone — do I taper?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2138-01-08 07:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No — you’re staying on 7.5mg daily. This is a maintenance dose for your condition, not a short-term taper."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2138-01-08 07:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks for all the help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2138-01-08 07:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and don’t hesitate to call if anything changes. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2138-01-08 07:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Have a good one, doc."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2138-01-08 07:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. Nurse will be in shortly with discharge papers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2138-01-08 07:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. Ready to get home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2138-01-05 21:43:00",
    "admission_end": "2138-01-08 15:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for post-procedural monitoring following a scheduled flexible bronchoscopy with balloon dilation and endobronchial biopsy for recurrent tracheal stenosis related to relapsing polychondritis. He tolerated the procedure well with no respiratory compromise. Post-procedural pain was managed with acetaminophen and oxycodone, and his symptoms improved over the hospital stay. He had mild bloody tracheal discharge, which was expected. Laboratory results showed elevated white blood cell count, attributed to inflammation rather than infection. Chest imaging before and after the procedure showed no complications such as pneumothorax. He was discharged home with a short supply of oxycodone, instructions to continue his chronic medications including prednisone and methotrexate, and follow-up appointments scheduled with interventional pulmonology, rheumatology, and infectious disease.",
    "problems": [
      "Relapsing polychondritis",
      "Other specified diseases of upper respiratory tract",
      "Other acute postprocedural pain",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Atrophy of testis"
    ]
  }
}
